description:
Develop a simple 2-bit binary switch-controlled LED driver. The module takes two switches (sw[0] and sw[1]) as inputs and uses a clock signal to update a 4-bit LED output. When sw[0] is low, the lower two bits of the LED output are set to zero; when sw[0] is high, they are set to binary '11' (3). Similarly, when sw[1] is low, the upper two bits of the LED output are zeroed; when sw[1] is high, they are also set to '11'. This allows control of the LED states based on the switch inputs.
module top_module(
    sw,
    clk,
    led
);

