description:
Design a circuit that functions as an 8-bit Gray code counter. It increments a binary counter on each rising edge of the clock input (CLK) while providing output in Gray code format. Upon receiving a reset signal (RST), the counter initializes to zero. The module converts the binary count to Gray code using the formula \( \text{Gray} = \text{Binary} \oplus (\text{Binary} >> 1) \), ensuring that only one bit changes between consecutive values, which is useful for error reduction in digital systems.
module top_module(
    input CLK,
    input RST,
    output reg [7:0] count_gray
);

code:
module top_module(
    input CLK,
    input RST,
    output reg [7:0] count_gray
);reg [7:0] count_binary;

    always @(posedge CLK or negedge RST) begin
        if (RST == 0) begin
            count_binary <= 8'b00000000;
            count_gray <= 8'b00000000;
        end
        else begin
            count_binary <= count_binary + 1;
            count_gray <= count_binary ^ (count_binary >> 1);
        end
    end

endmodule

