description:
Design a 32-bit multiplier block that processes a 32-bit input by effectively multiplying it by 256 while subtracting a product derived from the input. The circuit first calculates the input data and its left-shifts to achieve the necessary multiplications by 32 and 256. It generates a modified value through subtraction and then creates a final output by adding this modified value back to the original input, producing the resulting product in a 32-bit output. This module primarily functions as a specialized multiplier that integrates both addition and subtraction within its operation.
